      "content": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n\n    // Read matrix into flat array for better cache locality\n    std::vector<int> mat(n * n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &mat[i * n + j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Integral image: prefix sums with extra row/col of zeros\n    std::vector<int> pref((n + 1) * (n + 1), 0);\n\n    // First pass: compute row-wise partial sums in parallel\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        int row_sum = 0;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            row_sum += mat[i * n + j];\n            pref[(i + 1) * (n + 1) + (j + 1)] = row_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Second pass: accumulate column-wise to get true prefix sums\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n        int col_sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n            col_sum += pref[i * (n + 1) + (j + 1)];\n            pref[i * (n + 1) + (j + 1)] = col_sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    int mxSum = -2147483648; // minimum possible integer\n\n    // Search all top-left corners of SxS submatrices\n#pragma omp parallel for collapse(2) reduction(max:mxSum) schedule(runtime)\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n - s; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= n - s; ++j) {\n            int sum = pref[(i + s) * (n + 1) + (j + s)]\n                    - pref[i * (n + 1) + (j + s)]\n                    - pref[(i + s) * (n + 1) + j]\n                    + pref[i * (n + 1) + j];\n            if (sum > mxSum) mxSum = sum;\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Use integral image (prefix sums) for O(1) submatrix queries, parallelized with two-pass OpenMP work sharing during construction and collapse(2) reduction(max) schedule(runtime) during search. This leverages thread granularity via static scheduling on prefix passes and runtime-scheduled parallelism on the dominant search phase.",
  "notes": "Replaces sliding window with integral image for full parallelism. Prefix sums computed in two parallel passes (row-wise then column-wise). Search uses collapse(2) reduction(max) with schedule(runtime) to allow dynamic tuning of chunk sizes via OMP_SCHEDULE environment variable, aligning with role C focus on work sharing, reductions, scheduling and thread granularity.",
